---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Container from '../components/Container.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { site, socials } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base title="About" description="Reed Dadoune, software engineer.">
  <Container class="mt-16 sm:mt-32">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-y-16 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-rows-[auto_1fr] lg:gap-y-12">
      <div class="lg:pl-20">
        <div class="max-w-xs px-2.5 lg:max-w-none">
          <img
            src="/images/reed.jpg"
            alt="Reed Dadoune"
            class="aspect-square rotate-3 rounded-2xl bg-zinc-100 object-cover dark:bg-zinc-800"
          />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:order-first lg:row-span-2">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-800 sm:text-5xl dark:text-zinc-100">
          I&rsquo;m Reed Dadoune. I build things that run quietly.
        </h1>
        <div class="mt-6 space-y-7 text-base text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
          <p>
            I write software for the web, mostly backend and infrastructure. TypeScript and Node for
            the application layer, Docker and AWS underneath, and a persistent weakness for the kind
            of small utility that does one thing and then gets out of the way.
          </p>
          <p>
            Most of what I&rsquo;ve published started as a problem I hit on a real project: a docker
            ambassador that could actually resolve DNS, an asset manager for switching between dev
            and production bundles, a TypeScript implementation of Glicko-2. None of them are
            frameworks. All of them are short.
          </p>
          <p>
            The blog here is an archive. It covers 2014 through 2017, when I was writing up whatever
            I&rsquo;d just figured out about Thumbor, or Compose, or getting CodePipeline to deploy a
            static site. Some of it is genuinely dated now. I&rsquo;ve left the dates visible rather
            than quietly refreshing the posts, because a 2014 answer marked 2014 is more useful than
            a 2014 answer pretending to be current.
          </p>
          <p>
            This site is open source, like the last three versions of it were.{' '}
            <a
              href={site.repo}
              class="font-medium text-teal-600 transition hover:text-teal-700 dark:text-teal-400 dark:hover:text-teal-300"
              >The source is on GitHub</a
            >.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:pl-20">
        <ul role="list">
          {
            socials
              .filter((s) => s.icon !== 'mail')
              .map((s, i) => (
                <li class:list={['flex', i > 0 && 'mt-4']}>
                  <a
                    href={s.href}
                    class="group flex text-sm font-medium text-zinc-800 transition hover:text-teal-500 dark:text-zinc-200 dark:hover:text-teal-500"
                  >
                    <Icon
                      name={s.icon}
                      class="h-6 w-6 flex-none fill-zinc-500 transition group-hover:fill-teal-500"
                    />
                    <span class="ml-4">{s.label}</span>
                  </a>
                </li>
              ))
          }
          <li class="mt-8 flex border-t border-zinc-100 pt-8 dark:border-zinc-700/40">
            <a
              href={`mailto:${site.email}`}
              class="group flex text-sm font-medium text-zinc-800 transition hover:text-teal-500 dark:text-zinc-200 dark:hover:text-teal-500"
            >
              <Icon
                name="mail"
                class="h-6 w-6 flex-none fill-zinc-500 transition group-hover:fill-teal-500"
              />
              <span class="ml-4">{site.email}</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Container>
</Base>
